    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We start with the given expression \\((2x + 5)^2\\) and the value \\(x = 3\\).\n\nFirst, we substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n2x + 5 = 2(3) + 5\n\\]\n\nNext, we perform the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 3 = 6\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n6 + 5 = 11\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to square the result:\n\n\\[\n(11)^2 = 11 \\times 11\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(11 \\times 11\\), we calculate:\n\n\\[\n11 \\times 11 = 121\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{121}\n\\]",
